    <string name="help_start_title">Getting started</string>
    <string name="help_start_summary">The four sections and how they work together.</string>
    <string name="help_start_cellar">Every bottle you keep, grouped by wine. Search by name, producer, region, grape or vintage, and filter by style or by when to drink.</string>
    <string name="help_start_racks">Your racks, wine fridges and bins drawn as they look, so you know exactly where each bottle is.</string>
    <string name="help_start_tonight">What to open now: bottles at their peak or to drink soon first, and ideas to match a dish.</string>
    <string name="help_start_journal">The bottles you opened with your notes, the wines you discovered elsewhere, your shopping list and insights.</string>
    <string name="help_start_try_title">Try it</string>
    <string name="help_start_try">In **Settings**, load the sample cellar to explore every screen, then erase it when you are ready to add your own bottles.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_title">Adding bottles</string>
    <string name="help_adding_summary">A new wine, or more bottles of one you already have.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_existing_title">Already in your cellar?</string>
    <string name="help_adding_existing">Start typing the name: if the wine is already there, choose it and only enter how many bottles you add and where they go.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_wine">Only the **name** is required. The producer and the vintage help tell wines apart; leave the vintage empty for champagnes and blends without a year.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_style_title">Style and origin</string>
    <string name="help_adding_style">The style (red, white, sparkling…) is used for colors, serving temperature and food pairing. The appellation, region, country and grapes make search and pairing better.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_window">The years when the wine is at its best. It is estimated from the style and the vintage until you move the slider; enter the years from the producer or a guide if you know them.</string>
    <string name="help_adding_quantity_title">Quantity, size and location</string>
    <string name="help_adding_quantity">Add several bottles at once. Choose a rack to place them: the first free places are used unless you pick them. Without a rack, write where they are (kitchen, box in the garage).</string>
    <string name="help_adding_purchase_title">Purchase details</string>
    <string name="help_adding_purchase">Optional: price per bottle, date, shop or the person who gave it to you. Prices are used for the value of your cellar in Insights.</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_title">Label photos</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_summary">Fill in a wine from a photo of its label.</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_device_title">On this device</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_device">Take a photo of the label or choose one in the add form. Reading the label on the device itself is not available on Android yet; the photo is kept with the wine.</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_ai_title">With AI (optional)</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_ai">If an AI service is set up in Settings, the label photo is sent to it to fill in the name, producer, vintage, style, region, grapes and drinking window. Only that photo is sent, never your cellar.</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_typed_title">What you typed stays</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_typed">The AI only replaces fields that are empty or that were filled automatically. Everything you typed yourself is kept.</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_photo_title">The photo</string>
    <string name="help_scanning_photo">The label photo is kept with the wine, resized and without location data. You can change or remove it when editing the wine.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_title">Racks</string>
    <string name="help_racks_summary">Describe your storage so every bottle has a place.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_grid">One bottle per cell, in rows and columns. Choose **two bottles per cell** for racks deep enough to hold one behind the other.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_staggered">Every other row is offset by half a bottle and holds one fewer, like metal or terracotta racks. Enter the number of bottles in the widest row.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_shelves">Shelves holding a row of bottles, one to three deep. The dots under each bottle show which places are filled, front first.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_bins">Diamond bins or crates hold several bottles in a pile. Set how many bottles fit in each; tap a bin to see what is inside.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_places_title">Places</string>
    <string name="help_racks_places">Rows are lettered from the top and cells numbered from the left: **B3** is the second row, third cell. When a cell holds several bottles, **B3-2** is the second one (behind, or in the pile).</string>
    <string name="help_racks_moving_title">Moving bottles</string>
    <string name="help_racks_moving">Tap a bottle, then **Move**, then the new place (or press and hold a bottle). Tapping another bottle swaps them; a bin takes the bottle if it has room.</string>
    <string name="help_racks_irregular_title">Irregular racks</string>
    <string name="help_racks_irregular">Turn on **Rows of different lengths** for a rack under a sloped ceiling or a staircase, and set the length of each row.</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_title">Tonight and drinking windows</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_summary">When each wine is at its best.</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_maturity_title">Maturity</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_maturity">Each wine is **kept for later**, **ready**, **to drink soon** (last year of its window) or **past its peak**. The label and the symbol always say it, not only the color.</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_suggestions_title">Suggestions</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_suggestions">Tonight shows the bottles to drink soon first. Choose a dish to see the wines from your cellar that go with it, and why.</string>
    <string name="help_tonight_serving">Each wine page suggests a serving temperature and, for young full-bodied reds, how long to decant.</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_title">Drinking a bottle</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_summary">Keep track of what you opened and what you thought.</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_drink">Swipe a wine to the right, or use **Drink** on its page. The bottle leaves the cellar and its place in the rack becomes free. **Undo** appears for a few seconds.</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_note_title">Your note</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_note">Add a rating, a few words and the occasion, or open the full tasting note (appearance, nose, palate, finish, food). Everything is optional and can be edited later from the Journal.</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_gone_title">Given away, sold or broken</string>
    <string name="help_drinking_gone">Use **Given away, sold or broken** for a bottle that left the cellar without being drunk by you.</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_title">Discoveries and shopping list</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_summary">Remember wines you tasted elsewhere.</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_remember">At friends’, in a restaurant or on a trip, tap **Remember a wine** in the Journal and take a photo of the bottle. Add where you were, a rating, notes and tags.</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_tags">Tags group discoveries your way: gift ideas, for summer, to try again. Tap a tag to select it, or type a new one; tags you used before are suggested.</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_list">Turn on **To buy** to add the wine to your shopping list, with the price you saw. When you buy it, swipe it to the right (**Add to cellar**): it leaves the list once the bottles are added.</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_not_cellar_title">Not in the cellar</string>
    <string name="help_discoveries_not_cellar">Discoveries are not counted as bottles in your cellar and do not appear in racks or Tonight.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_title">Setting up AI</string>
    <string name="help_ai_summary">Use your own AI service for label recognition.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_provider_title">Choose a provider</string>
    <string name="help_ai_provider">In **Settings**, under AI label recognition, choose a provider. You need an account with it and an API key; the provider bills you directly for what you use, usually a fraction of a cent per label.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_key_title">Create a key</string>
    <string name="help_ai_key">Open the provider’s page with the link below the key field, create a key and paste it. The key is encrypted with the Android Keystore on this device and sent only to that provider.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_check_title">Check the key</string>
    <string name="help_ai_check">Tap **Check key and load models**: the app asks the provider which models your key can use and fills the model menu. Choose a model that reads images.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_local_title">Local server</string>
    <string name="help_ai_local">With Ollama or LM Studio on your computer, choose **Local server** and enter its address, such as `http://192.0.2.10:11434/v1`: on a phone or tablet, use the computer’s name or address on your network instead of localhost.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_url_title">Server URL</string>
    <string name="help_ai_url">Leave it empty to use the provider’s usual address. Change it only if the provider gives you another one, for example for its China region.</string>
    <string name="help_ai_sent_title">What is sent</string>
    <string name="help_ai_sent">Only the label photo, when you add a label photo or tap **Complete with AI**. Your cellar, notes and prices are never sent.</string>
    <string name="help_data_title">Backup, export and import</string>
    <string name="help_data_summary">Keep a copy and move your cellar.</string>
    <string name="help_data_backup_title">Back up</string>
    <string name="help_data_backup">**Export a backup (JSON)** saves everything: wines, bottles, racks, tastings and discoveries. Import it on another device, including an iPhone or a Mac, to restore it; nothing already there is replaced.</string>
    <string name="help_data_csv_title">Spreadsheet</string>
    <string name="help_data_csv">**Export a spreadsheet (CSV)** opens in any spreadsheet app, one line per bottle with its place. A CSV with at least a **name** column can be imported, including from another app.</string>
    <string name="help_data_photos_title">Photos</string>
    <string name="help_data_photos">Label photos stay on the device and are not included in backups yet.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_summary">Your cellar stays yours.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_1">Your cellar is stored only on your devices. There is no account, no tracking and no advertising.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_2">Sync between your devices and with the people you share a cellar with will be end-to-end encrypted: the server that relays changes will never be able to read them.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_3">The only data that can leave the device is the label photo, and only if you set up an AI service yourself.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_4">Encave is open source: anyone can check what the app does.</string>
